141 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/T (Landscape painting is the artistic representation of natural scenery. Such paintings often depict mountains, valleys, bodies of water, fields, forests, coasts, and may sometimes include man-made structures and people. While natural landscapes have been depicted in art since ancient times, the genre of landscape painting as an independent artistic tradition emerged in the Western tradition during the Renaissance in the 16th century. In the Eastern tradition, the roots of landscape painting can be traced back to 4th-century CE China.)
/E (Landscape painting is the artistic representation of natural scenery. Such paintings often depict mountains, valleys, bodies of water, fields, forests, coasts, and may sometimes include man-made structures and people. While natural landscapes have been depicted in art since ancient times, the genre of landscape painting as an independent artistic tradition emerged in the Western tradition during the Renaissance in the 16th century. In the Eastern tradition, the roots of landscape painting can be traced back to 4th-century CE China.)
